t for the financial creditors, referred to in clauses (a) and (b) of subsection (6A) of section 21, an application for initiation corporate insolvency resolution process against the corporate debtor shall be filed jointly by not less than one hundred of such creditors in the same class or not less than ten per cent. of the total number of such creditors in the same class, whichever is less.";}i:2;i:484;}i:18;a:3:{i:0;s:17:"listcontent_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:890;}i:19;a:3:{i:0;s:14:"listitem_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:890;}i:20;a:3:{i:0;s:13:"listitem_open";i:1;a:1:{i:0;i:2;}i:2;i:890;}i:21;a:3:{i:0;s:16:"listcontent_open";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:890;}i:22;a:3:{i:0;s:5:"cdata";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:421:" Provided further that for financial creditors who are allottees under a real estate project, an application for initiating corporate insolvency resolution process against the corporate debtor shall be filed jointly by not less than one hundred of such allottees under the same real estate project or not less than ten per cent. of the total number of such allottees under the same real estate project, whichever is less.";}i:2;i:896;}i:23;a:3:{i:0;s:17:"listcontent_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:1317;}i:24;a:3:{i:0;s:14:"listitem_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:1317;}i:25;a:3:{i:0;s:13:"listitem_open";i:1;a:1:{i:0;i:2;}i:2;i:1317;}i:26;a:3:{i:0;s:16:"listcontent_open";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:1317;}i:27;a:3:{i:0;s:5:"cdata";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:589:" Provided also that where an application for initiating the corporate insolvency resolution process against a corporate debtor has been filed by a financial creditor referred to in the first and second provisos and has not been admitted by the Adjudicating Authority before the commencement of the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (Amendment) Act, 2020, such application shall be modified to comply with the requirements of the first or second proviso within thirty days of the commencement of the said Act, failing which the application shall be deemed to be withdrawn before its admission.";}i:2;i:1323;}i:28;a:3:{i:0;s:17:"listcontent_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:1912;}i:29;a:3:{i:0;s:14:"listitem_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:1912;}i:30;a:3:{i:0;s:13:"listitem_open";i:1;a:1:{i:0;i:2;}i:2;i:1912;}i:31;a:3:{i:0;s:16:"listcontent_open";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:1912;}i:32;a:3:{i:0;s:5:"cdata";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:224:" Explanation. - For the purposes of this sub-section, a default includes a default in respect of a financial debt owed not only to the applicant financial creditor but to any other financial creditor of the corporate debtor.";}i:2;i:1918;}i:33;a:3:{i:0;s:17:"listcontent_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:2142;}i:34;a:3:{i:0;s:14:"listitem_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:2142;}i:35;a:3:{i:0;s:11:"listu_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:2142;}i:36;a:3:{i:0;s:14:"listitem_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:2142;}i:37;a:3:{i:0;s:13:"listitem_open";i:1;a:1:{i:0;i:1;}i:2;i:2142;}i:38;a:3:{i:0;s:16:"listcontent_open";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:2142;}i:39;a:3:{i:0;s:5:"cdata";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:151:" (2) The financial creditor shall make an application under sub-section (1) in such form and manner and accompanied with such fee as may be prescribed.";}i:2;i:2146;}i:40;a:3:{i:0;s:17:"listcontent_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:2297;}i:41;a:3:{i:0;s:14:"listitem_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:2297;}i:42;a:3:{i:0;s:13:"listitem_open";i:1;a:1:{i:0;i:1;}i:2;i:2297;}i:43;a:3:{i:0;s:16:"listcontent_open";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:2297;}i:44;a:3:{i:0;s:5:"cdata";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:305:" (3) The financial creditor shall, along with the application furnish - (a) record of the default recorded with the information utility or such other record or evidence of default as may be specified; (b )t he name of the resolution professional proposed to act as an interim resolution professional; and ";}i:2;i:2301;}i:45;a:3:{i:0;s:6:"entity";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:3:"(c)";}i:2;i:2606;}i:46;a:3:{i:0;s:5:"cdata";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:56:" any other information as may be specified by the Board.";}i:2;i:2609;}i:47;a:3:{i:0;s:17:"listcontent_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:2665;}i:48;a:3:{i:0;s:14:"listitem_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:2665;}i:49;a:3:{i:0;s:13:"listitem_open";i:1;a:1:{i:0;i:1;}i:2;i:2665;}i:50;a:3:{i:0;s:16:"listcontent_open";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:2665;}i:51;a:3:{i:0;s:5:"cdata";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:493:" (4) The Adjudicating Authority shall, within fourteen days of the receipt of the application under sub-section (2), ascertain the existence of a default from the records of an information utility or on the basis of other evidence furnished by the financial creditor under sub-section (3): 1 Provided that if the Adjudicating Authority has not ascertained the existence of default and passed an order under sub-section (5) within such time, it shall record its reasons in writing for the same.";}i:2;i:2669;}i:52;a:3:{i:0;s:17:"listcontent_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:3162;}i:53;a:3:{i:0;s:14:"listitem_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:3162;}i:54;a:3:{i:0;s:13:"listitem_open";i:1;a:1:{i:0;i:1;}i:2;i:3162;}i:55;a:3:{i:0;s:16:"listcontent_open";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:3162;}i:56;a:3:{i:0;s:5:"cdata";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:763:" (5) Where the Adjudicating Authority is satisfied that – (a) a default has occurred and the application under sub-section (2) is complete, and there is no disciplinary proceedings pending against the proposed resolution professional, it may, by order, admit such application; or (b) default has not occurred or the application under sub-section (2) is incomplete or any disciplinary proceeding is pending against the proposed resolution professional, it may, by order, reject such application: Provided that the Adjudicating Authority shall, before rejecting the application under clause (b) of sub-section (5), give a notice to the applicant to rectify the defect in his application within seven days of receipt of such notice from the Adjudicating Authority.";}i:2;i:3166;}i:57;a:3:{i:0;s:17:"listcontent_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:3929;}i:58;a:3:{i:0;s:14:"listitem_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:3929;}i:59;a:3:{i:0;s:13:"listitem_open";i:1;a:1:{i:0;i:1;}i:2;i:3929;}i:60;a:3:{i:0;s:16:"listcontent_open";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:3929;}i:61;a:3:{i:0;s:5:"cdata";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:132:" (6) The corporate insolvency resolution process shall commence from the date of admission of the application under sub-section (5).";}i:2;i:3933;}i:62;a:3:{i:0;s:17:"listcontent_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:4065;}i:63;a:3:{i:0;s:14:"listitem_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:4065;}i:64;a:3:{i:0;s:13:"listitem_open";i:1;a:1:{i:0;i:1;}i:2;i:4065;}i:65;a:3:{i:0;s:16:"listcontent_open";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:4065;}i:66;a:3:{i:0;s:5:"cdata";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:315:" (7) The Adjudicating Authority shall communicate- (a) the order under clause (a) of sub-section (5) to the financial creditor and the corporate debtor; (b) the order under clause (b) of sub-section (5) to the financial creditor, within seven days of admission or rejection of such application, as the case may be. ";}i:2;i:4069;}i:67;a:3:{i:0;s:17:"listcontent_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:4384;}i:68;a:3:{i:0;s:14:"listitem_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:4384;}i:69;a:3:{i:0;s:11:"listu_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:4384;}i:70;a:3:{i:0;s:6:"plugin";i:1;a:4:{i:0;s:12:"wrap_divwrap";i:1;a:2:{i:0;i:4;i:1;s:0:"";}i:2;i:4;i:3;s:7:"</WRAP>";}i:2;i:4385;}i:71;a:3:{i:0;s:6:"plugin";i:1;a:4:{i:0;s:12:"wrap_divwrap";i:1;a:2:{i:0;i:1;i:1;s:11:"half column";}i:2;i:1;i:3;s:18:"<WRAP half column>";}i:2;i:4394;}i:72;a:3:{i:0;s:4:"code";i:1;a:3:{i:0;s:1466:"
GOAL RULE IBC2016 "Initiation of CIRP by Financial Creditor" Section 7 PROVIDES
That the Initiation of CIRP by Financial Creditor under section 7 is allowed ONLY IF
  Section 7(1) applies AND
  Section 7(2) applies AND
  Section 7(3) applies AND
  Section 7(4) applies AND
  Section 7(5) applies


RULE IBC2016 Section 7(1) PROVIDES
Section 7(1) applies ONLY IF
     A default has occurred


RULE IBC2016 Section 7(2) PROVIDES
Section 7(2) applies ONLY IF
     the applicant apply in the prescribed Form and Manner AND
     the applicant apply with the prescribed fee


RULE IBC2016 Section 7(3) PROVIDES
Section 7(3) applies ONLY IF
     was the record of default evidenced from the records of IU OR
     was the record of default evidenced as specified by AA AND
     was the name of the RP proposed to act as an IRP AND
     was all other information (as specified by the Board) was provided


RULE IBC2016 Section 7(4) PROVIDES
Section 7(4) applies ONLY IF
     does the record of default ascertain the existence of a default from the records of the IU OR
     does the record of default ascertain the existence of a default on the basis of other evidence furnished by the FC under sub-section 7(3)


RULE IBC2016 Section 7(5) PROVIDES
Section 7(5) applies ONLY IF
     is the AA satisfied that a default has occurred AND
     is the application under sub-section 7(2) complete AND
     there is no disciplinary proceedings pending against the proposed RP


